WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.637
-As the U.S. passed a grim,
new coronavirus milestone,

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.639
and Texas continued
to dig itself out of

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.374
an unprecedented power crisis,

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:09.808
Fox News
and the Republican Party

00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:12.177
were laser-focused
on two things --

00:00:12.177 --> 00:00:14.847
lying about the Green New Deal
and the 2020 election.

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.516
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:21.220
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.456
It's been this way
for a long time,

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.758
but right now, in particular,
if you look around,

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.428
it's easy to feel like virtually
everything in our country

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.329
is broken.
The past year has been

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:33.133
one of ceaseless misery,
dysfunction, and chaos.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:36.269
And, yes, I know I'm starting
to sound like Werner Herzog

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.770
at the top of one
of these segments.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.606
[ German accent ]
Time is an unforgiving mistress.

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.275
She will lure you in
with her siren song,

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:44.977
her beauty disguising

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:48.314
her unquenchable thirst
for misery and death.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.949
[ Normal voice ] Werner,
you're scaring Baby Yoda.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.050
[ German accent ] Oh, sorry,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.986
I thought this was
a man-turtle puppet.

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:55.621
[ Normal voice ] Yesterday we
passed the horrific milestone

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:56.823
of half a million COVID deaths.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.025
Poverty and child hunger
are on the rise.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.527
Millions have lost
their health insurance.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.529
Grocery stores in Texas
are barren,

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:04.130
and Texans had to sit
in their cars

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.099
or start fires outside
just to keep warm.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.401 line:60%
If you have
a platform of any kind,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.070 line:64%
you can spend any time at all

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.804 line:60%
talking about
any of those things --

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:13.873 line:60%
things that matter
to real people's lives --

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.375 line:60%
or you could talk about
whatever the hell this is.

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:17.877 line:64%
-Did you see the dog?

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.612 line:60%
Let's -- I want to show you
something I noticed.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.281 line:60%
Doesn't he look a little, uh --
a little rough?

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:24.584 line:60%
[ Chuckles ]
I love dogs,

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.152 line:60%
but this dog
needs a bath and a comb

00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:28.921 line:64%
and all kinds of love and care.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:32.592 line:60%
I've never seen a dog in the
White House, uh, like this.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.761 line:60%
This dog looks like from --
I'm sorry -- from the junkyard.

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:37.129 line:64%
And I love that dog,

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.098 line:60%
but he looks like
he's not been well cared for.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:41.033 line:64%
-No, not not at all.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.701 line:60%
He looks very dirty
and disheveled

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:47.173 line:60%
and very unlike a presidential
dog like Millie or Victory

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:51.210 line:60%
or something else in the past
in the -- in the White House.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.247
-Is the "Max" in "Newsmax"
supposed to be ironic,

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.516
like they definitely
can't be maxing out on news

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.218
if they're talking about
Joe Biden's dog.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.986
Also, how out of touch
do you have to be

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.788
to think it's a good idea
to talk smack about dogs?

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:06.626
You know, who else can go
straight to hell? Paul Rudd.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.993
You know you're desperate
when the best attack

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.462
you can come up with
on a president

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.130
is claiming
he's got a janky dog.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.598
First of all, there's nothing
wrong with that dog.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:15.401
He looks great. That's how
a Biden dog should look.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.370
Joe Biden was never gonna have
a prize Pomeranian

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.271
named after
a Jane Austen character.

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:21.206
"Goddamn it, Mr. Willoughby,
sit still

00:02:21.206 --> 00:02:23.208
while I file your nails!"

00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:25.912
That dog looks like he'd be up
at 6:00, shoveling the driveway

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.914
and then packing his Milk-Bones
into a metal lunchbox

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.617
and heading to the mill.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.718
Just by looking at that dog,
you can picture how they met.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:35.788
Joe went into a local shelter,
either to use the restroom

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.490
or the pay phone to call Jill

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.059
and tell her he got kicked off
the quiet car again,

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.027
and he heard a whimpering
from a cage in the corner,

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:45.398
walked over and said, "Hey,
buddy, you remind me of me.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.832
You're not the best-looking
mutt in here,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.134
but you have a heart.
People always count you out,

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:52.238
but today I'm counting you in
to the Biden family."

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.706
And the dog was like,
"Can we go now?

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.009
And are you always gonna be
this long-winded?"

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.310 line:60%
Second, is there anything
more pathetic

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:00.179 line:60%
than a bunch of old pugs
calling a dog ugly...

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:03.549 line:60%
Andy Samberg?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.652
Instead of a set, Newsmax
just shoots their show

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.621
on the porch
of an old-timey drugstore.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:12.625
"The only thing uglier than her
disposition is her bloodhound."

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.227
So, that's a sample of what
the right-wing media

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.795
was spending time on,
amid a series

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.798
of urgent national crises,
exposing the potential

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.800
for even more disaster
down the road.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.870 line:0%
As "The New York Times"
put it...

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:42.255 line:0%
Man, the U.S. is starting to
feel like a sci-fi dystopia

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.390 line:0%
where Tilda Swinton plays
a blind oracle

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.025 line:0%
who knows the location of
the last remaining life crystal.

00:03:47.025 --> 00:03:49.395
I was leaning towards
making a "Mad Max" joke there,

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.730
but I didn't want to get
any more pronunciation notes

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.898
from Australians.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.031
[ Australian accent ]
It's actually pronounced

00:03:53.031 --> 00:03:55.868
"Mud Mix."
Good effort, though.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:58.737
Good on ya for tryin'.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:00.073 line:0%
[ Normal voice ]
Couldn't be blamed

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.774 line:0%
for reading
that "New York Times" passage

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.008 line:0%
and thinking it was describing

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:05.344 line:0%
some failed Soviet state
you never heard of.

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:07.346 line:0%
All we're missing is
a reclusive president-for-life

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:08.614 line:0%
who wears designer scarves

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:10.115 line:0%
and surrounds himself
with virgin guards.

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:12.551 line:0%
Although we got pretty close,
Trump did have Rudy,

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:14.787
who only ever got
to third base with his cousin.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.089
Sorry, it's true.
He married his cousin.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:19.525
And I never want to pass up
the chance to remind you

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.194
that the former president's
lawyer thought ancestry.com

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:24.363
was a dating site.
And I know

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:27.367
some Rudy defenders will say
it was his second cousin.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.069
And my response to that
is, "Okay."

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:34.073
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:37.276 line:0%
But this is very much
an American problem.

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.612 line:0%
The problem
is unfettered capitalism.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.847 line:0%
Texas is the only state
in the continental U.S.

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:43.082 line:0%
with its own power grid

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.616 line:0%
in order to avoid
federal regulation.

00:04:44.616 --> 00:04:47.286
And the state and local
governments have had trouble

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.455
getting people food
or safe drinking water --

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.791
in some cases,
running out of supplies.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.292
And by their own admission,

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:55.795
that's because they deferred
so much of their preparation

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.063
for crises like this
to the private sector.

00:04:58.063 --> 00:05:01.301 line:30%
-Bluntly, we have
very limited supply

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:04.036 line:30%
at the local government level
of cities

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.905 line:30%
that just have warehouses
full of bottled water

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.608 line:30%
that are owned by the city
or that have meals ready to eat

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:09.841 line:30%
that are owned by
the local government.

00:05:09.841 --> 00:05:11.210 line:36%
They usually don't exist.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.479 line:30%
We rely on the private sector
for our everyday needs.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.515
-Oh, yes, the private sector --
the same people who brought you

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:19.351
the Zune, Spirit Airlines,
and Jared Leto's Joker.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:20.652
You know, if I could
put Bernie in charge

00:05:20.652 --> 00:05:22.588
of one nonpolitical thing,
it would be that.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.623
[ As Bernie Sanders ]
We have too many jokers.

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:27.593
All you need is one joker.
That's more than enough jokes.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.296
Or everyone gets
their own Joker.

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:31.663
One or the other.

00:05:31.663 --> 00:05:33.099
[ Normal voice ]
So, by their own admission,

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.001
they rely on the private sector
for their everyday needs.

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:38.904
And I'm sorry, but I'm not sure
we should get our food and water

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.773
during crises
from the same people

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.074
who spent a week
[Bleep] their pants

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:43.276
when a bunch of Redditors

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:44.943
drove up the stock price
of a video-game store.

00:05:44.943 --> 00:05:47.012
If you could wreak havoc
on the markets

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:48.214
by telling your Internet buds

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.349
to buy stock in Blockbuster
as a goof,

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.685
maybe don't put those
same markets in charge

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:54.353
of -- I don't know --
electricity.

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.888
The private sector
can't be trusted

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:58.924
to provide everyone with the
basic material needs to survive.

00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:01.294
I mean, we still have 30 million
people without health insurance.

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.028
But don't worry,
the private sector has come up

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:05.430
with 7,000 different flavors
of Ejuice.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:08.401
Texas intentionally walled off
its power grid from regulation.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.302
In fact, they basically admitted

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:12.704
they'd rather have
a deregulated energy market

00:06:12.704 --> 00:06:15.040
run entirely by powerful
corporate interests,

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.609
even if that means suffering
through lethal storms

00:06:17.609 --> 00:06:19.445
without power, water, and heat.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.246 line:68%
-Former Texas Governor
Rick Perry says

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:25.017 line:68%
that Texans should be willing
to go days without electricity,

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:27.887 line:68%
a sacrifice they should make,
he says,

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:30.789 line:68%
to keep federal regulators
out of the state power grid.

00:06:30.789 --> 00:06:32.824
-I don't live in Texas,
but something tells me

00:06:32.824 --> 00:06:34.627
you don't speak for everyone
there, Rick Perry.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:37.096
I mean, he's like
the guy at the frat party

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:38.531
who thinks everyone's
got his back

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:41.166
when he stands up to the cops.
"We'd all rather go to jail

00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:43.001
than shut down this party,
coppers.

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:45.438
Right, guys?
Guys, why are the lights on?

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.805
Why are you turning -- Kyle?

00:06:46.805 --> 00:06:48.407
Are you draining
the Jell-O pool?

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:51.443
I spent all day
making that Jell-O, Kyle."

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:53.445
In their quiet moments,
they're honest about it.

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:56.849
They'd rather keep oil and gas
deregulated, in order

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:59.251
to serve the interests of their
powerful corporate patrons

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:01.520
in the private sector,
at the expense of actual Texans

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.756
who desperately need
and deserve help.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:07.092
But like clockwork, the Fox News
disinformation machine

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:10.162
went to work and blamed
the power outage in Texas

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:13.566
on a thing that does not
currently exist in any form

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:16.301
in Texas
or at the national level --

00:07:16.301 --> 00:07:17.469
the Green New Deal.

00:07:17.469 --> 00:07:19.505 line:15%
-Many are now blaming,
believe it or not,

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:22.307 line:15%
renewable green energy.
Wind turbines

00:07:22.307 --> 00:07:25.478 line:15%
in the Lone State --
Lone Star State are freezing.

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:26.879 line:15%
This shows how
the Green New Deal

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:29.648 line:15%
would be a deadly deal for
the United States of America.

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:31.950 line:53%
-Joe Biden and Democrats
better think twice about

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.253 line:53%
unleashing the Green New Deal
on the whole country.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:36.321 line:15%
-This is all more proof
that green energy

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:38.457 line:15%
just is not ready
for prime time.

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.192 line:53%
-These wind farms
that are frozen,

00:07:40.192 --> 00:07:41.928 line:53%
they're an eyesore,
they're not efficient.

00:07:41.928 --> 00:07:44.163 line:53%
-I mean, the bottom line is,
you had windmills that froze.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:47.233 line:53%
We have windmills
because of concepts and policies

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:49.167 line:53%
that come
from the Green New Deal.

00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:51.570 line:53%
-The lesson is,
we cannot go down

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:54.539 line:53%
this road, Laura,
of green energy.

00:07:54.539 --> 00:07:56.208 line:15%
-Unbeknownst to most people,
the Green New Deal

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:58.911 line:15%
came to Texas,
the power grid in the state

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.879 line:15%
became totally reliant
on windmills.

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:03.015 line:15%
How would you like
a massive power plant

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.350 line:15%
in your backyard,
humming and buzzing

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:08.787 line:15%
and chopping up birds?
That's what a wind turbine is.

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:11.857
-"How would you like a windmill
in your backyard,

00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:14.960
making noise, chopping up birds,
and sucking up all your air?

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.296
How would you like a windmill
to move in with you

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:19.098
and live with you
in your house,

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.967
eating all your food
and drinking all your booze?

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:22.434
How would you like that windmill

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:25.438
to get suspiciously close
with your wife,

00:08:25.438 --> 00:08:27.973
to the point where they start
going on shopping trips together

00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:29.374
without you,
leaving you at home,

00:08:29.374 --> 00:08:31.477
wondering what they're doing
together at the outlet mall

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:32.645
while you look out the window

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:34.613
at all the chopped-up birds
on your lawn?

00:08:34.613 --> 00:08:36.315
And how would you like
to come home

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:37.816
to find your wife's car
in the driveway?

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:39.852
But when you come inside,
you don't see her.

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.287
So you walk upstairs
to the bedroom,

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.822
and before you open the door,

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:47.159
the only noise you hear
is whoom, whoom, whoom?

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:48.494
[ Laughter ]

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:50.029
When my wife left me
for a windmill,

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:52.298
and it will happen to you, too."

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:54.967
Of course, it won't
surprise you to learn

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:57.837
that this lie is aggressively
mendacious and dumb,

00:08:57.837 --> 00:09:00.172
About 80% of the grid's capacity
this time of year

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.507
was forecasted
to come from natural gas,

00:09:02.507 --> 00:09:04.910
coal, and some nuclear power,
which of course, it does.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.245 line:76%
It's Texas.
They used to have

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:07.780 line:76%
a football team called
the Houston Oilers,

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.348 line:78%
not the Houston Solar Panels.

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:11.817 line:76%
And I'm sorry
that I have to say this,

00:09:11.817 --> 00:09:15.488
because it's insanely obvious,
because the New Deal --

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:17.323
the Green New Deal --
is not a thing

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:19.458
that exists in Texas
or at the national level.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.427
I mean, this is like blaming
your problems on "Avatar 2."

00:09:21.427 --> 00:09:23.061
It's not out yet.

00:09:23.061 --> 00:09:24.897 line:23%
The real problem
is that natural gas lines

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:27.266 line:23%
and instruments were frozen
by the severe winter weather,

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:29.468 line:23%
in part because they weren't
properly winterized.

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:31.703 line:60%
The state of Texas has left it
to power operators

00:09:31.703 --> 00:09:34.239
to decide to invest in
winterizing their equipment,

00:09:34.239 --> 00:09:36.141 line:0%
and many of Texas'
power generators

00:09:36.141 --> 00:09:37.409 line:0%
have not made those investments

00:09:37.409 --> 00:09:38.911 line:0%
necessary to prevent
disruptions.

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:42.414 line:0%
Meanwhile, only 7% of Texas'
forecasted winter capacity

00:09:42.414 --> 00:09:44.183 line:0%
is expected
to come from various

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:46.185 line:0%
wind power sources
across the state.

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:48.287
Kind of like how you can
only believe about 7%

00:09:48.287 --> 00:09:49.621
of what you see on Fox News.

00:09:49.621 --> 00:09:51.123
I mean, seriously,
can you imagine

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:53.325
how insane you have to be
to blame windmills

00:09:53.325 --> 00:09:56.628
and the Green New Deal
for a power outage in Texas?

00:09:56.628 --> 00:09:58.464
That's like blaming
Boston clam chowder

00:09:58.464 --> 00:10:00.899
for the smell in New Jersey.
It's not fair.

00:10:00.899 --> 00:10:03.969
They have their own reasons
for that smell.

00:10:03.969 --> 00:10:05.271
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:07.472
They don't have to go
out of state.

00:10:07.472 --> 00:10:09.975
These guys really expect us
to believe AOC snuck into

00:10:09.975 --> 00:10:11.744
the Houston oilfields
in the middle of the night

00:10:11.744 --> 00:10:14.813
and replaced all the derricks
with vegan food trucks.

00:10:14.813 --> 00:10:16.215
I mean, just think about that.

00:10:16.215 --> 00:10:18.050
Millions of Texans
were left without food,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.654
water, heat and electricity
in lethal temperatures for days

00:10:21.654 --> 00:10:23.923
in a state
that is known the world over

00:10:23.923 --> 00:10:26.325
as the U.S. epicenter
of oil and gas production.

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:28.327
And not only that, the people
who did manage

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:29.662
to keep the lights on
were stuck with

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:31.063
devastating electric bills,

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:33.765
thanks to surge pricing
imposed by the private sector

00:10:33.765 --> 00:10:35.100
Rick Perry cares so much about.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.402
A 63-year-old Army veteran

00:10:37.402 --> 00:10:39.872
who lives on Social Security
payments in a Dallas suburb

00:10:39.872 --> 00:10:42.974
was charged over $16,000.
I mean, that's horrifying.

00:10:42.974 --> 00:10:44.843
The only people who should ever
get an electric bill

00:10:44.843 --> 00:10:46.378
that's even half that much are

00:10:46.378 --> 00:10:48.147
those people with massive
Christmas displays

00:10:48.147 --> 00:10:50.082
synched up to
Trans-Siberian Orchestra.

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:52.184
So, not only
did the power go out

00:10:52.184 --> 00:10:54.653
at the epicenter of gas and
oil production in the country,

00:10:54.653 --> 00:10:57.255
but the people who are lucky
enough to keep their power

00:10:57.255 --> 00:10:58.858
had to drain their savings
to afford it.

00:10:58.858 --> 00:11:01.160
If that doesn't tell you
our country is broken,

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:02.561
then I don't know what will.

00:11:02.561 --> 00:11:05.297
The fact alone should prompt
some serious introspection.

00:11:05.297 --> 00:11:07.232
It's like if a Tom Cruise
movie bombed,

00:11:07.232 --> 00:11:09.101
that should never happen.
It would be a national disgrace.

00:11:09.101 --> 00:11:10.635
It would be on the front page
of every newspaper.

00:11:10.635 --> 00:11:13.239
The number-one trend on Twitter
would be #TomSnooze,

00:11:13.239 --> 00:11:14.840
and Congress would hold
emergency hearings

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.208 line:68%
to find out
how he got dragged into making

00:11:16.208 --> 00:11:18.644 line:68%
"Top Gun 3:
Goose is a Goose Now."

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:21.112 line:57%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:21.112 --> 00:11:23.149 line:53%
I mean,
I wouldn't not see it.

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:25.418 line:57%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:25.418 --> 00:11:27.987
Anyway, the point is,
it's a nightmare,

00:11:27.987 --> 00:11:29.288
and Texas desperately needs

00:11:29.288 --> 00:11:30.923
and deserves our immediate
help right now.

00:11:30.923 --> 00:11:32.924
It's also a cautionary tale
about climate change

00:11:32.924 --> 00:11:35.795
and emergency management,
deregulation, and overreliance

00:11:35.795 --> 00:11:37.429
on the private sector
and fossil fuels,

00:11:37.429 --> 00:11:39.598
as well as a warning about
our crumbling infrastructure

00:11:39.598 --> 00:11:42.000
and the criminal neglect
of our political class,

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.369
which has failed to ensure the
basic needs of every American

00:11:44.369 --> 00:11:46.004
are met,
as evidenced in part

00:11:46.004 --> 00:11:48.841
by one of the state's senators
fleeing to Cancún

00:11:48.841 --> 00:11:50.876
as his constituents froze
in their homes.

00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:52.678
Yikes.

00:11:52.678 --> 00:11:54.613
This is the most depressing
airport photo

00:11:54.613 --> 00:11:57.449
I've ever seen
that wasn't taken at LaGuardia.

00:11:57.449 --> 00:12:00.585
In fact, Ted Cruz is
the LaGuardia of people.

00:12:00.585 --> 00:12:03.455
With that beard, he looks like
an out-of-work osprey,

00:12:03.455 --> 00:12:05.023
too lazy to fly south
for the winter.

00:12:05.023 --> 00:12:07.859
He looks like Pavarotti
walked through a car wash.

00:12:07.859 --> 00:12:09.728
Then, once he was shamed
into coming back,

00:12:09.728 --> 00:12:11.096
Cruz tried to pretend

00:12:11.096 --> 00:12:13.065
he was actually interested
in helping out.

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:14.566
Saturday, he posted
photos of himself

00:12:14.566 --> 00:12:17.136
handing out bottled water
with the hashtag TexasStrong.

00:12:17.136 --> 00:12:19.671
Sure, dude,
we totally believe you.

00:12:19.671 --> 00:12:21.673
Ted Cruz is the husband
who sits on his couch

00:12:21.673 --> 00:12:23.242
watching football all day,

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:25.710
then sees his wife unloading
a car full of groceries,

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:28.013
waits until there's one bag
left in the trunk,

00:12:28.013 --> 00:12:30.716
then goes outside and says,
"Oh, uh, can I help?

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:32.150
[ Chuckles ]
Lucky for me,

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.154
just the paper towel bag.
Honey?

00:12:35.154 --> 00:12:37.222
Honey?"

00:12:37.222 --> 00:12:40.458
Whoom, whoom, whoom.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:40.458 --> 00:12:44.963
"Oh, Tucker, you weren't lyin'."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:44.963 --> 00:12:47.032
The problems we're facing
as a nation right now

00:12:47.032 --> 00:12:49.234
are structural.
They require radical solutions

00:12:49.234 --> 00:12:51.803
and they demand that we face
reality and tell the truth.

00:12:51.803 --> 00:12:53.739
And yet one of our two
major political parties

00:12:53.739 --> 00:12:55.674
is continuing to plunge deeper

00:12:55.674 --> 00:12:58.877
into an alternate universe
of delusion and disinformation.

00:12:58.877 --> 00:13:00.446
I mean, just consider the fact
that Donald Trump

00:13:00.446 --> 00:13:01.814
is no longer in office.

00:13:01.814 --> 00:13:03.448
He no longer holds
any real power

00:13:03.448 --> 00:13:04.816
over elected
Republican officials.

00:13:04.816 --> 00:13:07.118
He's the most unpopular
president in the history

00:13:07.118 --> 00:13:09.855
of polling, with a track record
of abysmal failure.

00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:13.258
And yet high-ranking Republicans
still refuse to say the obvious,

00:13:13.258 --> 00:13:16.228
which is that he legitimately
lost the 2020 election.

00:13:16.228 --> 00:13:19.597 line:60%
-Clear this up for me.
Joe Biden won the election.

00:13:19.597 --> 00:13:22.768 line:60%
He is the legitimate president
of the United States.

00:13:22.768 --> 00:13:25.404 line:60%
The election was not stolen.
Correct?

00:13:25.404 --> 00:13:29.307 line:60%
-Uh, look,
Joe Biden's the president.

00:13:29.307 --> 00:13:33.344 line:60%
There were a few states that did
not follow their state laws.

00:13:33.344 --> 00:13:36.915 line:60%
That's really the dispute
that you've seen continue on.

00:13:36.915 --> 00:13:38.917 line:60%
-But -- But, Congressman, I know
Joe Biden's the president.

00:13:38.917 --> 00:13:41.453 line:60%
He lives at the White House.
I asked you,

00:13:41.453 --> 00:13:43.755 line:60%
is he the legitimate president
of the United States?

00:13:43.755 --> 00:13:47.159 line:60%
And do you concede that
this election was not stolen?

00:13:47.159 --> 00:13:49.828 line:60%
Very simple question.
Please just answer.

00:13:49.828 --> 00:13:52.197 line:60%
-Once the elect -- Once
the electors are counted,

00:13:52.197 --> 00:13:53.798 line:60%
yes, he's
the legitimate president.

00:13:53.798 --> 00:13:56.702 line:60%
But if you're going to ignore
the fact that there were states

00:13:56.702 --> 00:14:00.105 line:60%
that did not follow their own
state legislatively set laws,

00:14:00.105 --> 00:14:02.040 line:64%
that's the issue at heart,

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.843 line:60%
that millions of people
still are not happy with.

00:14:04.843 --> 00:14:07.412
-First of all, that's not true.
Second, why are we

00:14:07.412 --> 00:14:09.515
still inviting these lunatics
on national TV?

00:14:09.515 --> 00:14:11.817
There should be
a basic litmus test.

00:14:11.817 --> 00:14:13.185
If you can't trust them
to be honest

00:14:13.185 --> 00:14:14.987
about something as simple
as who won the election,

00:14:14.987 --> 00:14:17.255
how can you expect them to be
honest about anything else?

00:14:17.255 --> 00:14:19.157
If my doctor walked into
the exam room

00:14:19.157 --> 00:14:21.293
with a copy
of the "Weekly World News"

00:14:21.293 --> 00:14:23.995
tucked under his arm and said,
"More bad news about Bad Boy;

00:14:23.995 --> 00:14:25.798
apparently he's the Pope's
secret love child,"

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:27.533
I wouldn't necessarily trust

00:14:27.533 --> 00:14:29.434
what he had to say
about my rash.

00:14:29.434 --> 00:14:33.472
And I need to get some feedback
on the rash!

00:14:33.472 --> 00:14:36.741
[ Laughter ]

00:14:36.741 --> 00:14:39.011
Scalise is the latest
high-profile Republican

00:14:39.011 --> 00:14:41.347
to fly to Mar-a-Lago
and curry favor with Trump.

00:14:41.347 --> 00:14:44.449
And in that same interview,
Scalise refused to even admit

00:14:44.449 --> 00:14:46.418
that Trump bore responsibility
for the insurrection

00:14:46.418 --> 00:14:47.552
on January 6th.

00:14:47.552 --> 00:14:50.255 line:60%
-When you met
with the former president,

00:14:50.255 --> 00:14:53.359 line:60%
did you ask him
to take responsibility?

00:14:53.359 --> 00:14:56.161 line:64%
Did he take responsibility?

00:14:56.161 --> 00:14:58.930 line:60%
-Well, Jonathan,
I was in Florida

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:00.265 line:64%
doing some fundraising

00:15:00.265 --> 00:15:01.633 line:60%
throughout a number
of parts of Florida.

00:15:01.633 --> 00:15:03.168 line:64%
I ended up at Mar-a-Lago,

00:15:03.168 --> 00:15:05.304 line:60%
and the president reached out
and we visited.

00:15:05.304 --> 00:15:08.073
-Wait, I'm sorry, how do you
just end up at Mar-a-Lago?

00:15:08.073 --> 00:15:10.075
Same way you end up
at a strip club?

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:11.910
"Honey, I didn't know
where the guys were going.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.512
We were drinking Sprite
and playing board games.

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:15.748
The next thing you know, we
ended up at The Diamond Donkey.

00:15:15.748 --> 00:15:17.883
I didn't want to be there, babe.

00:15:17.883 --> 00:15:21.153
I wanted to be pounding Sprites,
playing Risk."

00:15:21.153 --> 00:15:24.089
These election lies are
so insane that today

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:27.026
one of the chief disseminators
of the Big Lie, Mike Lindell --

00:15:27.026 --> 00:15:28.527
A.K.A., the My Pillow Guy --

00:15:28.527 --> 00:15:31.563
got sued for defamation
by Dominion Voting Systems

00:15:31.563 --> 00:15:34.199
for $1.3 billion --
$1.3 billion.

00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:36.201
Right now,
that dude's running around,

00:15:36.201 --> 00:15:38.303
shaking the change out of
every pillow in his house,

00:15:38.303 --> 00:15:39.571
which is no small amount
of money,

00:15:39.571 --> 00:15:41.806
as MyPillows
are filled with nickels.

00:15:41.806 --> 00:15:43.975
[ As Mike Lindell ] If it's good
enough for Thomas Jefferson,

00:15:43.975 --> 00:15:47.312
then it's good enough
for yours."

00:15:47.312 --> 00:15:49.715
"I'm Mike Lindell,
A.K.A. Mike the Pillow Guy."

00:15:49.715 --> 00:15:53.185
[ Laughter ]

00:15:53.185 --> 00:15:55.787
[ Normal voice ] Can you imagine
if that lawsuit succeeds,

00:15:55.787 --> 00:15:57.088
the company will have
to change its name

00:15:57.088 --> 00:15:58.691
to Dominion Pillows Inc.,

00:15:58.691 --> 00:16:01.326
and Lindell will just be
"a" pillow guy.

00:16:01.326 --> 00:16:02.828
Also, side note, why do
all these weirdos

00:16:02.828 --> 00:16:04.997
look like they haven't slept
in a hundred years?

00:16:04.997 --> 00:16:06.632
Ted Cruz looks like
a used MyPillow

00:16:06.632 --> 00:16:08.701
that was struck by lightning
and came to life.

00:16:08.701 --> 00:16:10.235
Did they all go to Cancún
for 36 hours?

00:16:10.235 --> 00:16:11.537
[ As Giuliani ] "I think
I got drunk

00:16:11.537 --> 00:16:13.038
and slept with my cousin."
[ Normal voice ] Rudy,

00:16:13.038 --> 00:16:15.574
that was nonalcoholic beer.
[ As Giuliani ] "Oh, no.

00:16:15.574 --> 00:16:17.709
Oh, I maybe did it on purpose.

00:16:17.709 --> 00:16:19.311
You guys,
she's my second cousin."

00:16:19.311 --> 00:16:21.012
[ Normal voice ] Why do you
think that makes it okay, Rudy?

00:16:21.012 --> 00:16:23.582
Why do you keep saying that
like we're all going to say,

00:16:23.582 --> 00:16:26.318
like, "Oh, our bad."
[ Laughter ]

00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:29.020
"We all owe Rudy an apology."
[ Laughter ]

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:30.922
This week
has demonstrated once again

00:16:30.922 --> 00:16:33.391
that we're facing a series
of towering crises,

00:16:33.391 --> 00:16:34.826
unprecedented in our lifetimes,

00:16:34.826 --> 00:16:36.961
that require bold action
and truth-telling.

00:16:36.961 --> 00:16:38.964
And yet one of our two
major political parties

00:16:38.964 --> 00:16:40.866
has become totally unmoored
from reality.

00:16:40.866 --> 00:16:42.101
They're lying about everything

00:16:42.101 --> 00:16:43.768
from the election
to the Green New Deal.

00:16:43.768 --> 00:16:45.670
And on top of that, they all
look like they could use...

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:48.740 line:60%
-A bath and a comb
and all kinds of love and care.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.608
This has been "A Closer Look."

